/-! # The `sha_final` region of `digest_file` in `sha256sum-min`

`digest_file` (0x402de0) inlines `sha_final`: after the read loop's last `read` returned 0
(`0x403034`, `Digest.AtPad`) it appends `0x80`, zero-fills the block (one block, or a second
block when fewer than eight bytes of room are left), stores the 64-bit big-endian bit length,
calls `sha256_compress` once or twice, and copies the eight state words out big-endian (the
`movzbl %ah,%ebx` at `0x4030e6` is the one instruction outside `X86.Ext`, an `Ext8` new form).

The region is `[0x403034, 0x40326e)`, 570 bytes (it also holds the error paths of
`digest_file`, which the segment never reaches and the listing omits). The listing covers the
78 instructions on the padding paths; the `X86.Ext` entries were produced by
`tools/x86-lift --raw`, the new form by hand, and all are re-checked by `SegVC.Listing.valid`
against the `Ext8` instance's decoder (`listing_valid`, by `decide`); `seg1_code` ties the
bytes to the loaded image.
-/

